WEBVTT

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:04.210
<i>The year is 2205 A.D.</i>

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:15.210
<i>To annihilate the History Retrograde 
Army, who scheme to alter history,</i>

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:17.850
<i>we, who were born from swords,</i>

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.160
<i>engage in mortal combat today as well!</i>

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.070
<i>Has Kane-san come this way, by any chance?</i>

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:43.370
<b>Touken Ranbu </b>Hanamaru<b></b>

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:59.390
"This anime is about the 
stories of the Hanamaru days

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:04.260
of a certain group of Sword 
Warriors in a certain citadel."

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:20.600
Again...

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:28.280
Duties are done.

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.040
I've eaten lunch.

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:31.250
That leaves...

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:32.390
Cherry blossom viewing!

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:34.130
31 - Ootachi
<b>Jiroutachi</b>

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:34.120
Oh! Great idea!

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:37.630
30 - Ootachi
<b>Taroutachi</b>

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:37.780
Didn't we view the cherry blossoms 
yesterday and the day before?

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:39.660
What are you talking about?

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:41.790
The cherry blossoms are 
blooming so splendidly.

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:45.130
Not viewing them would be 
an insult, wouldn't it?

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:50.510
Jeez, Jiroutachi...
You say such great things!

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:51.780
Don't I?

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:53.520
If that's the case...

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:57.160
We're viewing the cherry blossoms, everyone!

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:59.020
Gather underneath the tree!

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:00.090
Hey!

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:03.340
That's the sacred bell we got from Master.

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:05.520
It is not to be rung for 
cherry blossom viewing!

00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:06.890
I'm going, too!

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:07.830
Me, too!

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:09.050
Me, too!

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:10.500
See?

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:12.990
This bell is incredibly convenient.

00:03:13.970 --> 00:03:15.790
What, again?

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:18.550
29 - Wakizashi
<b>Horikawa Kunihiro</b>

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:18.550
A dream about the Ikeda Inn, huh?

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:20.090
Yeah.

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:22.100
And in Okita-kun's possession 
was definitely...

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:24.050
Yamatonokami Yasusada.

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:25.970
Me.

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:29.010
Y'know, I don't want to argue with a dream.

00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:32.390
But in reality it was Kashuu Kiyomitsu.

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:34.390
Then I wonder why?

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:36.510
Hey, hey, why?

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:38.510
It hasn't just been once or twice.

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:39.730
Hey, hey.

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:44.110
Isn't it just because you wanted to 
be the one he took to the Ikeda Inn?

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:45.230
That's not it!

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:47.730
Well, that's a lie.

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:51.170
But it was Kashuu Kiyomitsu 
he took that time.

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:54.410
I won't deny that was Okita-kun's choice.

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:58.500
It doesn't mean that you weren't necessary.

00:03:58.810 --> 00:04:00.370
He just chose me that day.

00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:01.660
That's all.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:04.990
Then, why do I keep having that dream?

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:06.070
It's me.

00:04:06.070 --> 00:04:07.030
Do you have a minute?

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:08.430
Sure.

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:10.650
Oh, it's Master's attendant.

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:14.270
Horikawa, you were made 
the secretary, right?

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:15.410
That's right.

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:16.560
I have a job for you.

00:04:20.290 --> 00:04:22.790
It is your first time as 
secretary so I'll tell you,

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:26.940
the Master of our citadel is 
a rare stay-at-home type.

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:27.870
They're chubby?

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:30.220
No, not chubby, stay at home.

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:32.740
They find it a pain to leave their room.

00:04:33.050 --> 00:04:37.130
For that reason, a shiki like this is 
imbued with the Sage's powers,

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:40.970
and someone else is able to manifest 
the Sword Warriors in their place.

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:43.590
<b>Sa</b>

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:42.900
With this?

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:46.720
So in other words, even though 
Master is actually shut inside,

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:49.220
they can manifest Sword 
Warriors at any time.

00:04:49.590 --> 00:04:50.790
Remember that.

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:55.510
We handle all the burden of labor so 
that our Master doesn't have to work—

00:04:56.740 --> 00:04:57.460
Huh?

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:01.070
I hope he comes soon.

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:03.610
Ah, Izuminokami Kanesada?

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:06.130
"Kane-san, Kane-san, Kane-san."

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:08.740
It's all he's been on 
about since he got here.

00:05:08.890 --> 00:05:10.390
Well, that's to be expected.

00:05:10.390 --> 00:05:13.300
I mean, they're both the proud 
swords of Hijikata-san.

00:05:14.670 --> 00:05:17.830
I'm sure he just wants to see 
him as soon as possible.

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:19.580
That's what it seems like.

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:23.710
Were you waiting for me, too, Kiyomitsu?

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:26.570
Stupid! It wasn't like that!

00:05:26.570 --> 00:05:28.910
How can you say something like 
that with such a straight face!

00:05:28.910 --> 00:05:30.330
It catches me off guard.

00:05:32.470 --> 00:05:35.180
Kane-san, Kane-san, Kane-san, 
Kane-san, Kane-san,

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:37.810
Kane-san, Kane-san, Kane-san, 
Kane-san, Kane-san!

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:39.270
<b>Sa</b>

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:53.330
32 - Uchigatana
<b>Izuminokami Kanesada</b>

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:48.870
I'm Hijikata Toshizou's beloved sword.

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:52.670
I'm a cool and strong sword who has 
recently become pretty popular,

00:05:52.670 --> 00:05:53.260
Izuminokami—

00:05:53.260 --> 00:05:53.880
Kane-san!

00:05:54.470 --> 00:05:56.410
At least let me finish!

00:05:56.780 --> 00:05:57.740
Kane-san!

00:05:57.970 --> 00:06:00.250
I'm sorry I made you wait, Kunihiro.

00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:04.090
Come with me, Kane-san.

00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:06.830
Ah, Hasebe-san!

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:08.280
So he finally showed up.

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:11.150
I am Master's attendant, Heshikiri Hasebe.

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:12.300
Nice to meet you.

00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:14.780
Yes, pleased to meet you, too.

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:19.160
If there is anything you are unsure of
regarding this citadel, feel free to ask me.

00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:21.090
Where's our new master?

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:23.260
Okay, I'll show you.

00:06:23.620 --> 00:06:24.790
It's okay.

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:26.200
I'll take him there.

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:27.740
This way.

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:28.600
Okay.

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:36.570
Horikawa looked happy.

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:40.320
Hey.

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:42.590
Where should I put this?

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:44.250
It's fine.

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:46.260
I'll take care of it later.

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:47.110
Okay.

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:50.650
As Sword Warriors,

00:06:50.650 --> 00:06:53.470
our duty is to protect history, huh?

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:56.270
You spoke with Master, didn't you?

00:06:56.650 --> 00:06:58.180
Is there something that's bothering you?

00:07:00.670 --> 00:07:01.480
Not really.

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:04.380
Hey, let's go back to our room.

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:05.230
Huh?

00:07:05.350 --> 00:07:07.370
We have our own room?

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:14.190
Kunihiro, tea.

00:07:14.190 --> 00:07:14.700
Okay!

00:07:24.430 --> 00:07:25.780
Okay, okay, okay!

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:28.460
Man, you're really thoughtful, aren't you?

00:07:29.790 --> 00:07:30.290
Okay!

00:07:30.290 --> 00:07:32.490
So thoughtful, it's scary!

00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:37.130
This place has a splendid tree.

00:07:37.240 --> 00:07:39.340
It's called the ten thousand 
leaf cherry tree.

00:07:39.340 --> 00:07:41.050
The ten thousand leaf cherry tree?

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:42.620
I've never heard of it.

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:47.680
I am told it is a miraculous tree that 
blooms only once in ten thousand years.

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:51.240
What's over there?

00:07:51.350 --> 00:07:52.410
The training hall.

00:08:03.110 --> 00:08:06.740
While a three-step thrust is usually 
done from the top to the bottom,

00:08:06.910 --> 00:08:09.880
he would thrust 
in the same exact place.

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:13.550
Apparently it was so fast that it only
looked like a single strike,

00:08:13.550 --> 00:08:15.090
so the enemy couldn't escape.

00:08:15.710 --> 00:08:17.810
Yeah, I remember that.

00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:18.600
Yo!

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:19.750
Sorry I kept you waiting.

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:20.880
As you know,

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:23.970
I am the beloved sword of the Shinsengumi's 
vice commander, Hijikata Toshizou.

00:08:23.970 --> 00:08:28.530
I'm a cool and strong sword who has 
recently become pretty popular. I'm Izu—

00:08:28.530 --> 00:08:29.260
Kane-san!

00:08:30.890 --> 00:08:31.780
Right.

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:33.950
Yasusada and Kiyomitsu...

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:35.660
So you guys got here first?

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:37.510
You were just late.

00:08:37.510 --> 00:08:38.280
Right?

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:41.410
I'm glad to see you.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:44.960
<b>Clear and Serene</b>

00:08:42.820 --> 00:08:44.950
Hijikata-san was scary, wasn't he?

00:08:45.210 --> 00:08:47.160
Well, he was practically a demon. A demon!

00:08:47.550 --> 00:08:49.670
"The Demon Vice Commander from Hell."

00:08:49.670 --> 00:08:51.300
Born a demon, and raised a demon.

00:08:51.450 --> 00:08:53.250
Demon-like guys are pretty—

00:08:53.700 --> 00:08:55.150
You bastards!

00:08:55.150 --> 00:08:57.450
You're bad-mouthing Hijikata-san too much!

00:08:57.450 --> 00:09:02.390
He purposely took on a hated role like 
that so he could manage the Shinsengumi!

00:09:02.390 --> 00:09:03.680
Right, Kunihiro?!

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:06.270
What are you laughing for?!

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:15.870
So this is where you guys 
have been training.

00:09:16.140 --> 00:09:20.060
The Shinsengumi headquarters had a 
wonderful training hall, too, didn't it?

00:09:20.060 --> 00:09:24.180
Let me ask you this, though.
Why are you guys fighting?

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:27.400
That's because, as Sword Warriors,
we have to stop the History Retrograde Army—

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:29.360
So you just go whenever Master tells you to?

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:31.810
That's exactly like a dog.

00:09:32.260 --> 00:09:36.690
Hijikata-san fought to the end for 
the shogunate and for the world.

00:09:36.910 --> 00:09:39.380
We've been brought here like this,

00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:42.160
but for who and what reason 
are we fighting?

00:09:42.410 --> 00:09:44.070
That must be worked out.

00:09:44.420 --> 00:09:47.100
I want to be strong like Okita-kun.

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:50.880
That's why I fight,
because I love Okita-kun.

00:09:51.420 --> 00:09:55.380
I admire him, and he was incredibly 
skilled with a sword.

00:09:56.710 --> 00:09:59.860
I want to become stronger and 
protect Okita-kun's fate.

00:10:00.880 --> 00:10:04.110
You want to become stronger 
like Okita-kun, huh?

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:05.740
I see.

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:09.870
I saw you training earlier, and your 
sword skills still need some work.

00:10:10.020 --> 00:10:11.030
All right!

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:15.230
Why don't you face off with 
someone cool and strong like me?

00:10:15.550 --> 00:10:16.570
Whaddya say?

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:19.590
I accept.

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:23.180
<b>Clear and Serene</b>

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:24.840
Now then.

00:10:24.840 --> 00:10:30.080
The Tennen Rishin Style includes 
fencing, jujitsu, bojitsu, and then...

00:10:30.580 --> 00:10:31.650
Umm...

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:32.520
Iai.

00:10:32.790 --> 00:10:33.840
Iai.

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:36.490
It's a martial art that can do 
anything when those are combined.

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:39.650
When it comes to striking, 
I think of Hijikata-san.

00:10:39.650 --> 00:10:40.570
Isn't that right?

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:41.760
It is!

00:10:42.470 --> 00:10:46.080
Hijikata-san used me constantly 
for quite a long time.

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:50.830
Normally, because a sword handle is held 
firmly by the pinky and the ring finger,

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:53.040
the pinky is always 
the first to get injured.

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:57.460
However, with my handle, he would get 
hurt near his index finger and thumb.

00:10:57.820 --> 00:11:01.560
That's because every time he would strike 
he'd put all his strength in his index finger.

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:04.850
His striking stance would 
defeat swords crosswise.

00:11:05.070 --> 00:11:07.960
He would strike once quickly, like lightning.

00:11:08.220 --> 00:11:10.570
It didn't matter if there 
was a response or not.

00:11:10.750 --> 00:11:14.780
He'd draw his sword again 
with lightning speed.

00:11:15.770 --> 00:11:18.960
And the first strike would increase 
to the second and third times.

00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:23.700
The Tennen Rishin Style is a style 
of limitless possibilities.

00:11:27.780 --> 00:11:29.710
All right, let's practice!

00:11:30.490 --> 00:11:33.740
Though practicing with real 
swords isn't bad, either.

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:36.110
It's because it's training.

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:37.680
I've said that many times.

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:39.650
Really come at me.

00:11:39.650 --> 00:11:41.690
So as not to disappoint me.

00:11:41.810 --> 00:11:45.080
I'll strike true, even 
without you egging me on.

00:11:47.460 --> 00:11:48.600
Well then,

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:49.350
begin!

00:11:54.770 --> 00:11:57.370
I've been training with Kiyomitsu every day.

00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:03.230
It can do anything!

00:12:03.230 --> 00:12:05.540
That's the Tennen Rishin style!

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:09.470
Hey now, two against one?

00:12:09.570 --> 00:12:11.290
You said anything, right?

00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:24.730
That's enough. I'll just go myself.

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:32.960
Damn it!

00:12:33.150 --> 00:12:36.170
If only I'd been the one to get here first.

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:38.300
What's going on here?

00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:39.980
What is it, a fight?

00:12:40.120 --> 00:12:43.730
Hey, you are to refrain from 
sparring here with real swords!

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:02.260
You said you wanted to get 
stronger like Okita, right?

00:13:03.850 --> 00:13:06.960
Then, what was Okita's strength?

00:13:09.480 --> 00:13:10.690
Okita-kun's...

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:12.260
Is that story true, Okita-san?

00:13:12.690 --> 00:13:14.760
You're so funny, Okita-san.

00:13:14.760 --> 00:13:17.680
Your sword skills aren't the only 
thing about you that's top-notch.

00:13:17.870 --> 00:13:21.730
Okita-san, Okita-san, Okita-san, 
Okita-san, Okita-san, Okita-san!

00:13:21.730 --> 00:13:22.720
Kane-san!

00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:23.310
Right!

00:13:24.060 --> 00:13:26.830
Double sword attack!

00:13:41.350 --> 00:13:42.450
Hey, now...

00:13:42.450 --> 00:13:44.300
You just got here, so don't overdo it.

00:13:50.050 --> 00:13:52.230
That didn't turn out so great.

00:13:52.230 --> 00:13:57.610
Well, for us to meet again like this, that 
must mean there's a meaning to fighting.

00:13:59.820 --> 00:14:01.850
You seem like you've remembered something.

00:14:05.460 --> 00:14:06.610
<i>I did.</i>

00:14:06.740 --> 00:14:09.340
<i>Okita-kun's strength wasn't 
just in his sword.</i>

00:14:09.690 --> 00:14:14.280
<i>He also had the strength to make those 
around him feel light and warm.</i>

00:14:15.050 --> 00:14:16.320
<i>I wonder if I can do that.</i>

00:14:16.680 --> 00:14:18.240
<i>Like Okita-kun.</i>

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:19.660
By the way...

00:14:19.660 --> 00:14:20.530
Who are you?

00:14:20.530 --> 00:14:21.440
He's...

00:14:23.040 --> 00:14:24.510
I'm sorry for the delay.

00:14:24.510 --> 00:14:27.880
I am the beloved sword of the Shinsengumi's 
Vice Commander, Hijikata Toshizou.

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:31.970
I'm a cool and strong sword who has 
recently become pretty popular.

00:14:32.370 --> 00:14:33.460
I'm Izuminokami—

00:14:33.460 --> 00:14:35.460
Yo! Demon Vice Commander from Hell!

00:14:36.580 --> 00:14:39.580
You two keep doing that on purpose!

00:14:39.720 --> 00:14:40.580
Ow!

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:43.980
<b>Touken Ranbu </b>Hanamaru<b></b>

00:14:44.960 --> 00:14:48.910
You two keep doing that on purpose!

00:14:53.230 --> 00:14:55.780
This place has a splendid tree.

00:14:55.910 --> 00:14:57.920
It's called the ten thousand 
leaf cherry tree.

00:14:57.920 --> 00:14:59.410
The ten thousand leaf cherry tree?

00:14:59.840 --> 00:15:01.250
I've never heard of it.

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:20.890
Because I was not in this 
world for a long time,

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:24.900
I did not think that outside 
scenery was so splendid.

00:15:29.770 --> 00:15:32.400
Jiroutachi-san, you reek of alcohol.

00:15:32.400 --> 00:15:33.830
What are you saying?

00:15:33.830 --> 00:15:35.110
It's a wonderful smell.

00:15:35.420 --> 00:15:38.730
When the cherry blossoms are this 
beautiful, it can't be helped.

00:15:38.900 --> 00:15:41.130
So you're saying I can't drink?

00:15:41.130 --> 00:15:45.220
Where is it written that I can't drink 
underneath the cherry blossoms?

00:15:45.220 --> 00:15:47.990
Then who let me get drunk?

00:15:48.250 --> 00:15:50.540
That was you, rice wine-chan!

00:15:53.440 --> 00:15:57.420
The relationship between us is one 
of mutual love and affection.

00:15:57.420 --> 00:16:02.240
My body's components are exactly 
the same as the rice wine.

00:16:08.050 --> 00:16:09.080
Ororo?

00:16:09.440 --> 00:16:11.780
Hey! Shokudaikiri-kun!

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:13.690
Bring some more rice wine!

00:16:14.130 --> 00:16:16.440
I told you that was the 
last of it, didn't I?

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:20.750
I know that coming to this world 
has been a brilliant feeling,

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:24.460
but the liquor has run dry because we've 
been drinking it almost every day.

00:16:26.200 --> 00:16:28.930
There you have it, Jiroutachi.

00:16:29.610 --> 00:16:34.860
The phrase that I didn't want to hear
the most was the alcohol has run out.

00:16:34.960 --> 00:16:37.290
Someone please go buy more alcohol.

00:16:37.860 --> 00:16:39.620
Jiroutachi is seriously ill!

00:16:39.620 --> 00:16:42.070
At this rate his divinity 
is going to run out!

00:16:42.070 --> 00:16:44.270
Would someone mind going 
to the general store?

00:16:44.270 --> 00:16:45.620
Then, I'll go!

00:16:45.620 --> 00:16:46.970
Atsushi, let's go.

00:16:46.970 --> 00:16:48.500
Okay, sure.

00:16:48.730 --> 00:16:49.970
I'll go, too!

00:16:50.280 --> 00:16:52.320
Make sure you go to Master's room first

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:54.910
and get permission to go 
to the general store.

00:16:54.910 --> 00:16:55.960
Yes!

00:16:54.910 --> 00:16:55.960
Okay!

00:16:57.720 --> 00:16:59.330
Thank you, General.

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:01.510
We'll be careful on our trip!

00:17:02.290 --> 00:17:06.250
<b>General Store</b>

00:17:02.850 --> 00:17:04.240
We've arrived!

00:17:04.240 --> 00:17:06.250
Okay, let's hurry and get it, and get back.

00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:08.590
They sell everything!

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:10.850
Oh, dango!

00:17:10.850 --> 00:17:12.310
Let's buy some for everyone.

00:17:12.310 --> 00:17:14.430
Ah, Atsushi-niisan, that's...

00:17:14.540 --> 00:17:16.700
I'm not sure what to buy.

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:19.650
Okay, then, let's buy three 
for now and eat them.

00:17:19.650 --> 00:17:21.300
W-We can't.

00:17:21.300 --> 00:17:23.390
Let's by what we're 
supposed to and go back.

00:17:23.390 --> 00:17:24.520
What's this?

00:17:23.390 --> 00:17:38.870
<b>General Store</b>

00:17:24.520 --> 00:17:26.540
Atsushi, I want this.

00:17:26.540 --> 00:17:27.950
Guess it can't be helped.

00:17:27.950 --> 00:17:31.020
Then I'll get one of these.
Doesn't it look cool?

00:17:31.020 --> 00:17:33.130
Eh, does it look cool?

00:17:33.130 --> 00:17:36.700
We're going to make Hasebe-san mad if 
we buy things we're not supposed to.

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:38.620
It's fine, it's fine.

00:17:39.260 --> 00:17:40.810
We're back!

00:17:40.810 --> 00:17:42.110
Welcome back!

00:17:42.110 --> 00:17:43.570
Jeez, I've been waiting!

00:17:43.760 --> 00:17:46.800
So, what did you guys buy—

00:17:47.600 --> 00:17:48.740
This!

00:17:48.740 --> 00:17:50.870
It's called a "face pack."

00:17:50.870 --> 00:17:52.940
Doesn't it look like Ichi-nii?

00:17:52.940 --> 00:17:54.180
Uh...

00:17:54.340 --> 00:17:57.220
<b>Osaka Castle</b>

00:17:54.680 --> 00:17:55.840
Look at this!

00:17:55.840 --> 00:17:57.210
It's a pennant!

00:17:58.170 --> 00:17:59.880
And, what about you, Maeda?

00:17:59.880 --> 00:18:02.090
You made sure to buy the sake, right?

00:18:02.090 --> 00:18:03.050
Yes!

00:18:03.280 --> 00:18:04.600
Here it is.

00:18:06.500 --> 00:18:07.870
My apologies.

00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:10.560
We wanted alcohol, not salmon (<i>sake</i>).

00:18:12.590 --> 00:18:14.490
Look! Jiroutachi!

00:18:14.490 --> 00:18:15.900
Boo-hoo-hoo!

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:18.750
Then I'll go buy the alcohol!

00:18:18.860 --> 00:18:21.330
I worry about you on your own.

00:18:21.330 --> 00:18:22.820
I'll go with you.

00:18:22.820 --> 00:18:25.630
What? I'll be fine!

00:18:25.620 --> 00:18:27.370
<b>General Store</b>

00:18:27.370 --> 00:18:28.640
Ah! I want this!

00:18:28.640 --> 00:18:30.590
And this! Ah, and this!

00:18:30.590 --> 00:18:33.120
Is it really a good idea to covet so much?

00:18:33.570 --> 00:18:35.910
Ah, this is really nice!

00:18:35.910 --> 00:18:36.800
So is this!

00:18:36.800 --> 00:18:38.090
What do you think?

00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:40.910
Do you want to see everyone's happy faces?

00:18:41.100 --> 00:18:49.560
<b>Lunch Box</b>

00:18:41.380 --> 00:18:44.140
Ah, that's right! You're hungry, aren't you?

00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:46.740
Let's buy ten lunch boxes 
and take them back!

00:18:46.740 --> 00:18:49.560
I pray that you won't get scolded 
for wasting money on them.

00:18:49.790 --> 00:18:52.030
What are you going to buy, Nikkari-san?

00:18:52.200 --> 00:18:53.960
Let's see...

00:18:55.610 --> 00:19:00.490
<b>Fufufufufu...</b>

00:18:58.790 --> 00:19:00.270
What's that?

00:19:02.190 --> 00:19:03.320
We're back!

00:19:03.590 --> 00:19:04.790
We have presents.

00:19:04.930 --> 00:19:05.710
The alcohol?

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:08.080
We have something better than that.

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:09.970
Go on, try pushing it.

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:15.170
<b>Fufufufufu...</b>

00:19:15.320 --> 00:19:17.060
It's a laughing bag.

00:19:17.060 --> 00:19:20.180
Doesn't that laugh remind 
you of someone else?

00:19:21.440 --> 00:19:23.920
It's rather quite interesting.

00:19:24.560 --> 00:19:27.810
<b>Fufufufufu...</b>

00:19:28.010 --> 00:19:30.070
What the hell is this?!

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:34.020
Octopus, squid, conger eel, 
young yellowtail, fin meat, tuna, eggs,

00:19:33.810 --> 00:19:36.520
You guys can't do anything, can you?

00:19:34.020 --> 00:19:36.520
herring roe, salmon roe, amberjack, mackerel,

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:38.910
Jiroutachi, leave your alcohol to me!

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:39.530
yellowtail, albacore belly,
ark shell, pickled red ginger!

00:19:39.160 --> 00:19:41.160
Now, let's go, Yamanbagiri.

00:19:41.910 --> 00:19:43.570
Me?

00:19:54.270 --> 00:19:57.090
As I thought, this suits me the best.

00:19:57.270 --> 00:19:59.120
Yamanbagiri! Smile!

00:20:01.230 --> 00:20:02.540
Did it take?

00:20:06.650 --> 00:20:08.220
Let's buy this and go back.

00:20:08.440 --> 00:20:09.520
I'm fine.

00:20:13.260 --> 00:20:14.980
I don't need anything.

00:20:18.620 --> 00:20:19.680
You...

00:20:21.370 --> 00:20:22.440
What is that...

00:20:26.690 --> 00:20:28.910
Ah, this is bad! Mitsubou!

00:20:28.910 --> 00:20:31.400
Jiroutachi-san, leave it to us!

00:20:31.400 --> 00:20:33.900
We'll hurry and get your alcohol!

00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:35.880
You just want an excuse
to go, too, don't you?

00:20:36.760 --> 00:20:39.360
That's right. We've run out of eggs.

00:20:39.360 --> 00:20:42.510
If I'd known I was going to do this,
I would've checked the refrigerator.

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:48.030
Oh! Hey, isn't this the flower doll with 
glasses that Yamanbagiri had earlier?

00:20:48.030 --> 00:20:49.590
Why is it wearing glasses?

00:20:50.630 --> 00:20:51.930
It's evening!

00:20:51.930 --> 00:20:53.430
So that's what it is!

00:20:53.430 --> 00:20:57.870
They're glasses that let you practice 
for night battles even during the day!

00:20:57.870 --> 00:20:59.570
That could be it.

00:20:59.570 --> 00:21:06.530
<b>General Store</b>

00:21:00.140 --> 00:21:02.250
This makes it like evening.

00:21:02.250 --> 00:21:03.880
They suit you, Mitsubou.

00:21:03.880 --> 00:21:05.020
You think so?

00:21:05.020 --> 00:21:06.260
Thank you, Tsuru-san.

00:21:06.530 --> 00:21:09.490
Nevertheless, why did you buy all of them?

00:21:09.710 --> 00:21:12.360
I thought everyone else might want some, too.

00:21:12.670 --> 00:21:15.260
That's enough. I'll just go myself.

00:21:18.610 --> 00:21:20.330
What's going on here?

00:21:20.330 --> 00:21:22.220
What is it, a fight?

00:21:22.390 --> 00:21:23.530
Jeez.

00:21:24.500 --> 00:21:28.340
Hey, you are to refrain from 
sparring here with real swords!

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:31.930
<b>General Store</b>

00:21:36.900 --> 00:21:40.110
<b>Sake</b>

00:21:37.150 --> 00:21:39.790
Jirou-san has revived!

00:21:40.120 --> 00:21:42.050
Jeez, you two...

00:21:42.180 --> 00:21:43.060
Ow!

00:21:46.380 --> 00:21:48.050
You're the new guy, right?

00:21:48.050 --> 00:21:49.930
Now, drink up!

00:21:49.930 --> 00:21:51.400
You stink!

00:21:51.400 --> 00:21:52.570
Now, now, come here!

00:21:52.570 --> 00:21:54.370
Get off of me!

00:21:54.370 --> 00:21:55.950
I'm sorry my brother is trouble.

00:21:55.950 --> 00:21:58.590
Okay, okay! First, one drink!

00:22:20.150 --> 00:22:24.940
<b>Gifts for you, Master</b>

00:23:54.990 --> 00:23:59.990
<b>More Hanamaru Next Week!</b>
